<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      User BFF schema. Liquibase runs over a JDBC datasource (Liquibase has no
      R2DBC runner); all runtime data access goes through R2DBC. Every table is
      owner-keyed by the Casdoor JWT subject (user_id) — a user only ever touches
      their own rows (owner-enforcement lives in the service layer too).

        001 — user_profile     (own profile: gender/pronouns/tz/displayName/visibility/vanity)
        002 — user_preference  (own per-key preferences incl. home-guide-dismissed)
        003 — user_block       (own self-blocks pushed to Matrix/Mastodon/internal)
        004 — user_profile.vanity_username + reserved-name CHECK (vanity collision guard)
        005 — enum/domain CHECK constraints (DB parity for the API-enforced
              user_profile.visibility + user_block.platform vocabularies)
        006 — self_silence (self-service visibility hide; NOT a ban — zero Casdoor
              roles / access_suspension / revocation keys; @Scheduled auto-clear)
        007 — media_poison_decision (server-owned AI-cloak decision + outcome for
              the BFF media-proxy: audit + badge + repost source of truth)
        008 — user_profile.screen_reader_name (ASCII-only a11y aria-label name;
              defaults from an ASCII display_name, prompted when display_name is
              non-ASCII)
        009 — connected_client_audit (owner-scoped record of the user's OAuth apps /
              device sessions on the homeservers + revoke audit)
        010 — domain scoping: a `domain` column (DEFAULT 'default', NOT NULL) on every
              owner-keyed table = the brand/tenant the row belongs to, derived
              server-side from the validated token issuer (DOMAIN_<x>). A principal
              only sees/mutates rows in its own domain; SUPERADMIN is unscoped.
              Back-compat: existing rows + single-issuer clusters are all 'default'.
        011 — user_preferences_store: the DURABLE per-user UI preferences store the
              /bff/user/preferences endpoint reads/upserts. Domain-FIRST: the brand is
              part of the composite PK (user_id, pref_key, domain) so a multi-brand
              owner keeps a separate, owner-isolated preference per brand (carries the
              per-user media.poison.default the compose AI-poison toggle persists).
        012 — notifications PR1: the in-app notification FLOOR
              (user_notifications) + per-category PREFERENCES
              (notification_preference). Both owner-keyed (user_subject) + domain-
              scoped; prefs MIRROR 011 (domain-first composite PK). account-restriction
              is FORCED-ON (un-silenceable) — API-coerced + a DB CHECK backstop. SHIPS
              DARK: nothing writes user_notifications yet (the snapdragon-actions
              reconciler in a later PR is the only writer); this is the read/prefs side.
    -->

